mit pulsatory currents; also, a reed acted on by pulsatory currents by means of an electromagnet, and hence made to respond to the vibrations of a corresponding reed sending these currents from a distance. See ''harmonic telegraph'', under ''telegraph''.—'''2.''' In the reed-organ, one of the reeds by which the tone is produced. —'''3.''' In ''printing'', an inking-roller that has a vibrating as well as a rotary movement, which aids the distribution of ink on the inking-table of a cylinder-press.

